                <pb facs="0494" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1115/3046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Valencia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Valencia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-24T18:00:00-04:30">February 24, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A … C. R …, departmental passport 362,797, deserter from the Spanish Army, has
                    applied to the Consulate for protection and assistance in returning to the
                    United States. He has not been arrested <pb facs="0495" n="483" xml:id="pg483"/>
                    but may at any moment. He declares he did not take oath of allegiance or other
                    promise. He is in great danger. Please instruct as to protection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
